  "2026-11-11T05:32:04.866Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Confirmed current npm latest is 2026.11.11 and updated the locked published oracle. Baseline differential runs precede native changes. Centralize refusal recovery, scope and redaction; retain byte comparisons and all existing cases."
  "2026-11-11T05:50:02.157Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Baseline against 2026.11.11: 120 differential tests, 59 passed and 61 failed (claim target 20 passed and 7 failed). Additional drift includes compact TOON list/null columns, complete omission receipts, newest-first compact history with total/order echoes, actual-format intent estimates, exclusive activity windows, relationship root-evidence ordering, close completion provenance and close recovery retries. All existing byte and durable-state comparisons remain exact; stale claim-attribution expectations now assert the published warning and successful durable transition."
  "2026-11-11T06:11:46.818Z",codex-rust164-1111,"The expanded orientation pass reached 25 of 32 passing before the final shared fixes: matching-active test health, root-edge cost reservation and incident-root edge ordering. All 397 library unit tests pass; the focused CLI/bin/parity run then passed 44 binary tests, 18 CLI dispatch tests and 14 parity contracts. Corrected the final ownership fault expectation to require the published warning. Running all eight differential targets through linked pm tests, sequentially, with each cargo command capped at 1200 seconds and two test threads."
  "2026-11-11T06:37:56.618Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Full differential rerun exposed additional shared compact-envelope drift: TOON brief/search metadata, relationship-bound omission declarations, and configured lifecycle fallback. Correcting producers and the common renderer while retaining exact stream comparisons. Close, conformance and list targets already pass; scoped credential and ownership provenance regressions pass focused checks."
  "2026-11-11T06:54:18.241Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Behavioral reverts in disposable copies: replacing only refusal credential projection with a no-op fails the scoped credential differential; reverting only ownership_error_json fails the ownership-provenance differential; reverting only TOON table encoding fails the small-search differential. Each failure was an assertion failure, and all scratch functions were restored. The fixed scoped test passes in both JSON and human output; the final full differential run will recheck all three tests. Clippy and fmt pass. The previous envelope gate passed 504 tests; refreshing it after the final human-output correction. Aggregate release-check runs the full suite twice including branch coverage, exceeding the requested 45-minute budget based on measured target durations; CI retains unchanged aggregate thresholds."
  "2026-11-11T06:58:13.088Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Final claim/release differential: 29 passed, 0 failed, including both new credential/scope and ownership-provenance regressions after restoration. The shared renderer now matches human Held by provenance as well as JSON envelopes. No differential test was skipped or loosened. Remaining differential targets and the final envelope refresh continue sequentially."
  "2026-11-11T07:27:55.872Z",codex-rust164-1111,"The complete interim rerun reached 118 passed and 4 failed: one unchanged five-second relationship deadline, one Unicode intent-budget/continuation case, and two later search-limit TOON cases. Prepared source fixes now cache exact packet shapes across recovery probes, apply canonical cost precedence and finalized-envelope overhead through the same intent projection, and format numeric filter echoes with JavaScript number semantics. The Unicode test follows the emitted producer cursor with --after and independently exercises snapshot compaction while retaining its exact stream, SDK, surrogate-pair and tail-count assertions. No budget assertion or byte comparison was loosened. Rechecking these changes before another full run."
  "2026-11-11T07:35:07.439Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Focused positive checks now pass both output-parity tests and the unchanged relationship five-second deadline. The added cache unit test proves exact JSON/TOON byte counts across numeric-width boundaries; clippy and fmt pass. Refreshed four independent behavioral reverts all fail at assertions: credential projection, ownership envelope construction, TOON table encoding, and canonical intent-budget preparation. All scratch changes were restored. Running every differential target again, then the complete envelope gate, with unchanged timeouts and at most two configured test threads."
  "2026-11-11T07:55:56.404Z",codex-rust164-1111,"The cache counter boundary now has a fifth independent behavioral revert proof: resetting only its starting width chooses 999 instead of the published 1000 fixed point and fails the exact rendering unit assertion. All five scratch reverts were restored. Final search, orientation, output-parity and pagination targets have passed; the affected orientation target will be refreshed once more after the counter correction, and the envelope gate includes the strengthened unit test."
  "2026-11-11T08:12:47.696Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Final verification complete: every differential target passes, 122 passed and zero failed/ignored (including two new refusal regressions), versus the initial 59 passed and 61 failed across 120 tests. The final orientation refresh passes all 32 after the counter-width correction. Envelope gate: 505 passed, zero failed/ignored (398 lib, 44 binary, 18 dispatch, 11 ownership, 14 parity, 20 release-pipeline). Clippy and fmt pass; five independent behavioral reverts fail as expected and were restored. Exact commands and per-target counts are recorded in docs/NATIVE_PARITY_2026_11_11.md. Measured differential runtime is about 30 minutes, so the aggregate normal and coverage passes exceed the requested 45-minute local limit; CI must certify unchanged aggregate/coverage thresholds and other platforms. Potential published auditability regression: claim/start can succeed with an attribution warning while the same stale session lock still refuses release. No upstream issue was filed. Releasing the claim without closing the task."
  "2026-11-11T11:34:41.726Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Round 2: reproduce admission CI failures; enumerate every oracle-backed Rust and crash-harness target; address review findings with exact oracle evidence, bounded cache retention and regression corpora. Preserve all byte/state assertions and append-only history. Review threads remain for the orchestrator to answer."
  "2026-11-11T12:08:33.482Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Admission baseline reproduced: nine passed and three failed. Restoring scalar structured refusal defaults and captured preview scaffold defaults gives twelve passed with unchanged admission assertions. Focused atomic custom-terminal, stored credential, scoped string-only retry, partial human failure, positional close-scope and mixed-precision activity regressions pass. The conservative oracle-backed inventory contains twenty-one Rust targets including indirect Node/SDK consumers and metadata guards; linked all missing commands and running every target sequentially with the required published CLI, twenty-minute caps and two threads."
  "2026-11-11T12:20:31.832Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Independent credential review added a stored whitespace-only username control alongside stored whitespace passwords and escaped copies. Ordinary prose handles, emails outside URLs and URL path/query/fragment separators retain their receipts. Published 2026.11.11 still leaks stored whitespace passwords and over-redacts public path separators; native output is hardened for the explicitly requested privacy boundary. Published positional scope parsing after the separator, lexical mixed-precision activity ordering, and JSON omission of partial-success explanation are documented in the review evidence; no upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-11-11T12:44:03.368Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Complete Rust gate results: all twenty-one oracle-backed targets pass, 216 target tests total including 125 differential tests, with zero failed or ignored. Admission is twelve passed versus the reproduced nine passed and three failed. The envelope gate passes 512 tests: 399 lib, 48 binary, 20 dispatch, 11 ownership, 14 parity and 20 release-pipeline. Clippy and fmt pass. Parity/release substring matching also reran the combined envelope commands; counts are unique target counts. Independent disposable-copy reverts and restored positives are running before final crash checks and a refreshed claim differential."
  "2026-11-11T12:49:47.027Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Eleven independent disposable-copy behavioral reverts failed at assertions, never compilation: persisted credential enrollment, URL authority boundary, linear cache retention, configured terminal start, positional recovery scope, string-only scoped retry, partial-failure human why, activity instant comparison, scalar admission output, preview defaults and crash pin. Every same command passed again after restoration; finally blocks restored all scratch functions and the main worktree was never mutated. The TOON 256-token change adds an exact coverage case to unchanged production behavior, so no changed production function exists for that row to revert. Full pagination passes the new case. Detailed evidence is in the review receipt."
  "2026-11-11T13:01:29.670Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Crash gate exposed an additional shared acknowledgement drift: 87 passed and three failed after the oracle pin was accepted. Published CLI comments now include a one-based index in returned comment entries; native durable item/history bytes already match exactly. Updated only the native CLI comment receipt builder to add those indexes, preserving the existing legacy wrapper and all crash equality assertions. Fresh claim differential passes all thirty tests. Refreshing envelope, lint and full crash gates after the receipt fix, and adding an independent receipt-function revert proof."
  "2026-11-11T13:12:51.139Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Final round-two validation: all twenty-one oracle-backed Rust targets pass (216 unique tests, including 125 differential), all twelve unchanged admission tests pass, and the refreshed envelope gate passes 512. The receipt fix also passes all other contract refreshes. Complete crash gate: ninety passed, zero failed/skipped; TypeScript, ESLint, history-prefix and retained-evidence guards pass. Clippy and fmt pass. Twelve independent production-function or constant reverts fail at assertions and the same commands pass after restoration, including the added comment receipt producer proof. Exact commands, counts, thread map and oracle discrepancies are in docs/ORACLE_REVIEW_2026_11_11.md. Aggregate normal plus coverage runs exceed forty-five minutes; unchanged aggregate and platform certification remain with CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/165/checks. Release the claim for orchestrator verification without closing the task or Dependabot PR."
  "2026-11-11T14:43:45.530Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Round 3: read all six requested review threads in full. Close the multi-URL credential projection class across registration and every emitted refusal field and stream. Probe the pinned oracle for delimiter placement, both budget controls, invalid activity cutoffs and JSON partial-step explanations; fix only measured parity gaps or retain an evidenced compatibility decision. Record the explicit public-URL divergence described by upstream issue 1707. Preserve every existing differential assertion and append-only tracker history."
  "2026-11-11T15:02:56.958Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Round-three oracle evidence: numeric output_budget=3000 accepts legacy token_budget abc, 255, 256 and 1000, so retain canonical precedence instead of introducing an oracle-incompatible refusal. The new exact JSON/TOON corpus passes. The oracle omits partial-step why in JSON while retaining it in human output; the unchanged exact claim test already enforces both. Invalid context clocks refuse with unknown_error, exit one and Invalid time value, not an argument-error envelope; native now matches those exact bytes and accepts equivalent RFC3339 offsets. Delimited close recovery inserts evidence immediately after close and before the delimiter; native matches JSON and human bytes, and both emitted retry arrays successfully close a real non-git fixture with identical receipt, item and history bytes. Global multi-URL unit and actual process stream corpora pass, including public scoped-package URLs and slash-bearing passwords from issue 1707."
  "2026-11-11T15:05:57.358Z",codex-rust164-1111,"The retry replay was verified after correcting the probe to locate the Issue fixture in its configured folder: both emitted argv arrays complete successfully with identical stdout receipt, item and history bytes. The conservative twenty-one-target oracle inventory is running through exact linked-test indexes to avoid the prior substring-selection duplicates. Each command retains the twenty-minute cap and two test threads; envelope, clippy, fmt and complete crash checks follow sequentially. Behavioral reverts will run only in a disposable copy after these gates."
  "2026-11-11T15:39:34.921Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Round-three verification complete: all twenty-one oracle-backed Rust targets pass, 219 tests including 128 differentials, zero failed/ignored. Envelope gate: 514 passed (399 library, 49 binary including six credential tests, 21 CLI dispatch, 11 ownership, 14 parity, 20 release-pipeline). Complete crash check: ninety passed, zero failed/skipped, with TypeScript, ESLint, history-prefix and retained-evidence guards. Clippy and fmt pass. Six independent function reverts failed at assertions, and every same command passed after restoration: global URL scan, every-password registration, close flag placement, close human mode, close human envelope and invalid context cutoff. The two compatibility decisions retain oracle JSON omission and numeric-budget precedence, with exact passing tests. All six requested thread texts were read; fifteen threads were returned, seven unresolved including one outdated accepted finding. Intentional issue-1707 divergence, commands, measured counts and controls are documented in docs/NATIVE_PARITY_2026_11_11.md. Aggregate coverage and other platforms remain for CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/165/checks. Releasing the claim without closing the item or review threads."
  "2026-11-11T17:24:18.078Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Round 4: retain the accepted round-three work and audit atomic lifecycle admission against separate claim/start. Reproduce strict blocker and coincident open/progress fallback defects in non-git fixtures, factor one shared admission/status-resolution function used by atomic and separate starts, compare exact oracle bytes and no-write refusals, and audit other composed lifecycle paths. Preserve differential assertions, append-only history and all gate thresholds. The prior CI cancellation was orchestrator automation; the next push starts fresh CI."
  "2026-11-11T17:57:44.837Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Measured non-git fixtures now match the pinned oracle for strict explicit and ranked blocker refusals without item/history/session writes, coincident or invalid progress selectors, dependency aliases, closed/missing/external blockers and warn/off/force policies. Shared lifecycle_admission::admit_lifecycle_transition runs under the actual claim/update lock for atomic starts, explicit preflight and update, and pause updates. Ranking is advisory: a real blocker reopening after a captured ready candidate is independently checked at the atomic writer, matching SDK claim-next exhaustion context. The composition audit also fixed pause/release-pause entering the effective progress status when its configured open status is the fallback. Close-plus-release invokes both guarded operations; no start-plus-close composition exists. A source-audited remaining race difference is the published explicit-start release compensation when a blocker opens between commits; native retains its successful claim with partial-step recovery. No late-blocker compensation was added without a complete ownership/history proof. All 16 existing review threads and 16 comments were read; there is no thread pagination."
  "2026-11-11T17:58:19.520Z",codex-rust164-1111,"A newly arrived review thread about long intent cursors is outside round-four lifecycle scope. Search found no matching open follow-up; tracked as pm-rust-long-intent-cursor, tagged gh:unbraind/pm-rust#165. No cursor behavior is claimed fixed or independently reproduced in this round."
  "2026-11-11T18:04:21.101Z",codex-rust164-1111,"The full claim/release differential passes 38/38 (reviewed head had 30). The newly requested mutation_contract gate exposed two pre-existing frozen close-history expectations: 27 passed, 2 failed because they lacked the published completion context and corresponding record hash. Replayed the identical five-operation recipe through the pinned published CLI in a non-git tracker: the first four history records match every frozen byte; the fifth adds context.completion timestamp/source and its measured record hash. Updated only that oracle-derived literal and provenance comment; all existing assertions stay exact. The separate live conformance target passes 2/2."
  "2026-11-11T18:11:13.675Z",codex-rust164-1111,"Round-four validation is complete: claim_release_differential 38, mutation_contract 29 after the measured frozen-fixture refresh, conformance_differential 2, close_differential 7, admission_contract 12, and combined envelope/lifecycle gate 515 (400 library, 49 binary, 21 dispatch, 11 ownership, 14 parity, 20 release-pipeline): 603 full-target passes, zero failures or ignored tests. Clippy and fmt pass. Each gate retained its 1200-second cap, two Cargo jobs and two test threads. Six independent function reverts failed behaviorally with exit 101 and no compilation failures: explicit blocker, ranked blocker, stale-ranked reopened blocker, explicit fallback, ranked fallback, pause fallback admission. Every exact same command passed after restoration in finally; reverts never changed the package worktree. Read all 16 review threads/16 comments and all 23 open items; initial context returned 10 and keyword search 10/58. Shared admission/status resolver: lifecycle_admission::admit_lifecycle_transition. Remaining composition compensation is tracked in pm-rust-start-claim-compensation; the unrelated cursor thread is tracked in pm-rust-long-intent-cursor. No other omitted composed admission was found. Aggregate normal-plus-coverage release validation exceeds the established 45-minute budget; platform and coverage certification remain with fresh CI after push. No new upstream issue or regression was filed. Keep this item in progress for orchestrator verification and release only this authors claim."
  "2026-11-12T01:12:39.843Z",codex-agent,"Round 5: synced remote head 75dc318 and confirmed main is already contained. Read all 22 review threads and all 12 unresolved comments without pagination, the latest CodeRabbit review (no Outside diff range section), and the two independent blocking lifecycle probes. Fix additive schema admission, unverifiable blocker policy, complete blocker IDs, nested-scheme credential projection, intent cursor and receipt finalization classes, and isolate alias-only coverage. Revalidate existing measured review decisions instead of redoing accepted fixes. Add behavioral regressions and function revert controls, inspect aggregate coverage gaps at the unchanged 100 percent thresholds, and run targeted Rust, harness typecheck/lint and repository identity/self-host/changelog checks with 1200-second caps and at most two workers. Keep all items open and release this claim before stopping."
  "2026-11-12T01:29:33.766Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed and fixed the additive-status registry loss, exact stored blocker-ID lookup, invalid UTF-8 classification and its warning/force bypass through lineage. Strict/warn/force/off encoding differentials now pass and preserve the corrupt bytes. New refusal scanning tests cover nested schemes and copied password fragments across shared projection; existing multi-URL and public-URL controls remain. Oracle probes confirm final declaration feasibility must use the stabilized estimate and invalid output cursors must precede omitted-result recovery. The long producer-cursor finding is valid in both native and the pinned oracle: the oracle emits a truncated ellipsis cursor. Repairing native replay under this final round creates an explicit documented continuation-safety divergence; every existing byte comparison remains intact. Reusing pm-rust-long-intent-cursor for that fix. The latest review contains no Outside diff range findings."
  "2026-11-12T01:41:39.700Z",codex-agent,"The isolated alias-only fixture exposed a real recovery-command drift: the fields list must be quoted as one argument. Fixed the common unblock renderer and retained the exact oracle stream assertion. Current writes canonicalize depends_on, so the test keeps a historical alias spelling after removing the scalar and canonical edge, then asserts a no-write refusal. The old ordinary-claim corpus validation contract remains strict; only an already-admitted start can omit unverifiable lineage documents after the shared blocker policy has allowed them. Added corpus tests for duplicate/encoding/document policy, warning scope, mixed ranked outcomes, sparse TOON and human recovery. Beginning a split instrumented coverage pass with every command capped at 1200 seconds and two workers; all thresholds and source inclusion remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-12T02:53:49.967Z",codex-agent,"Round-five class review now covers additive status replacement by normalized ID, cached selection roles, exact legacy blocker identity, typed UTF-8 strict/warn/force/off policy, and the admitted lineage reread. Stored blocker titles also register credential fragments before shared refusal projection. Disposable-copy behavioral reverts are running; all prior exact assertions remain intact. The discovery coverage run completed 27 integration targets; three failures exposed a stale performance matcher, monotone intent feasibility and external role overrides, all corrected and focused reruns passed."
  "2026-11-12T03:00:18.118Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof is complete: 13 independent controls produced assertion failures with only the relevant function or source matcher reverted, and the identical focused command passed after restoration in each disposable copy. Controls cover additive schemas, typed UTF-8 policy, admitted lineage, full blocker IDs, nested URL spans, stored producer credential fragments, long cursors, cursor validation before omission, final receipt feasibility, quoted unblock advice, alias-only admission, ranked status aliases and the performance harness matcher. The first feasibility differential alone did not discriminate the old function, so a direct final-receipt boundary corpus now supplies its negative control. All final controls pass."
  "2026-11-12T03:17:58.558Z",codex-agent,"Fresh instrumented claim/release passes 41/41, close passes 8/8, and the alias-only fixture passes after removing every masking edge. Coverage review added real filesystem disappearance schedules for recursive and fallback blocker reads, preserving fatal I/O policy under force. It also removed unreachable guards after typed comment/list classification and complete credential registration; behavioral must-allow and privacy corpora remain intact. Tracker strict health passes after reinstalling pinned merge drivers; historical advisory records were preserved."
  "2026-11-12T03:36:02.586Z",codex-agent,"Final-source static gates pass: Cargo check, clippy, fmt, TypeScript typecheck and ESLint, plus private-item documentation. The compiled build-script contract passes and measures both GNU and MSVC branches without exclusions. Release-pipeline contracts pass 21/21. Audit passes with the existing allowed unmaintained unsafe-libyaml warning. Search is the last large instrumented target; a final unit and affected-target refresh follows before the push."
  "2026-11-12T03:45:20.527Z",codex-agent,"All 27 integration targets now pass in the instrumented pass; the library target is also oracle-backed through the stale-ranked-start test. Independent pinned-oracle reproduction confirmed a stored blocker title fully redacts its credential URL but leaves a copied password visible (start_blocked_by_open_dependency, exit 4). Native deliberately redacts that copied fragment too; this privacy divergence is documented beside the public-URL and executable-cursor divergences. No upstream issue was filed. Final unit/CLI refresh includes both output streams, real filesystem disappearance and final-receipt budget boundaries."
  "2026-11-12T05:01:34.131Z",codex-agent,"The final library and binary unit targets pass 429/429 and 57/57; CLI dispatch passes 24/24. Changed library modules now measure 100 percent lines, functions, regions and branches at unchanged thresholds. Frozen finalized-budget cases use 3236 tokens for omission and 3237 for the adjacent must-allow; valid snapshot replay also refuses correctly after the second projection changes row bytes. Real SDK close, intervening force-claim and release operations cover distinct-field receipt accounting, and fallible comment serialization has an explicit serializer-failure control. Final CLI dispatcher coverage runs and refreshed function reverts remain before the push."
  "2026-11-12T05:41:55.249Z",codex-agent,"Round-five final source: all 22 review threads enumerated; all 12 unresolved threads and their 12 comments read completely, no remaining pages. Latest CodeRabbit review body has no outside-diff findings. Runtime status schemas merge additive entries; blocker IDs resolve fully before shorthand; invalid UTF-8 follows strict/warn/force/off policy and admitted starts retain warnings through lineage reads. Shared refusal projection registers stored producer credentials and nested schemes. Cursor validation precedes omission, producer cursors remain executable, final intent feasibility only downgrades. Historical alias-only fixtures, normalized selection roles and the performance matcher are covered. JSON why additions, legacy-budget rejection under a canonical budget, and argument-error classification of invalid activity cutoffs are declined using exact oracle evidence. Thread map and commands: docs/ORACLE_REVIEW_ROUND5_2026_11_12.md."
  "2026-11-12T05:41:56.335Z",codex-agent,"Final validation: 815 Rust tests pass (429 library, 58 binary, 328 across all 27 integration targets), zero failed or ignored; oracle inventory includes the library and all 21 oracle-backed integration targets (235 integration tests). Eight differential targets: original 59 passed/61 failed; final 143 passed/zero failed. Final coverage passes unchanged thresholds: lines 18745/18745, functions 1922/1922, regions 30539/30539, branches 4256/4256. Check, clippy, fmt and private-item docs pass. just crash-check passes typecheck, lint, 90 Node tests, history-prefix and 21-receipt/37-reference evidence checks; restored performance harness passes 25 tests. Identity integration passes 7 tests; dependency audit passes under the existing advisory policy. Every gate is capped at 1200 seconds and tests use at most two workers. Full normal plus instrumented suite durations exceed the permitted 60-minute local aggregate window; fresh CI must certify just release-check and other platforms. Follow final-head checks at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/165/checks."
  "2026-11-12T05:41:57.197Z",codex-agent,"Final-source revert proof refreshed in disposable copies: all 13 negative controls fail behaviorally and all 13 exact same commands pass after restoration. Eleven controls restore baseline-equivalent function/source behavior: additive schema, typed UTF-8, admitted lineage, complete blocker ID, nested URL span, producer credential registration (both unit and process streams), producer cursor preservation, cursor-before-omission, final receipt feasibility, quoted unblock advice, and performance source matcher. Two sensitivity controls disable existing depends_on admission and normalized ranked roles; they prove isolated fixtures discriminate those paths. The first exact feasibility comparison alone passed its revert, so a finalized-receipt boundary test now supplies the discriminating proof. No compilation failure is counted. Intentional oracle divergences: public scoped-package URLs stay intact, long producer cursors execute, and copied stored-password fragments are removed. The independent oracle still exposes the copied password after redacting its URL; no upstream issue was filed. Existing explicit-start compensation risk remains tracked separately. No assertion, coverage threshold or exclusion was weakened; no review thread was answered or resolved."
  "2026-11-12T05:47:25.703Z",codex-agent,"Final health boundary: the exact CI command node tests/oracle/launch.mts health --check-only --require-merge-drivers --strict-exit passes, as does the seven-test identity target. A supplementary full-history probe reports the two existing chain mismatches already tracked by pm-rust-b4yl; all four affected files are byte-identical to origin/main. Added evidence to that existing follow-up instead of creating a duplicate. The check-only health pass is not a full historical-integrity certification. Both known histories remain append-only. Final Rust receipts remain 815 passed and all four aggregate coverage percentages 100."
