  "2026-11-13T06:43:45.055Z",codex-agent,"Round 12 complete: all six requested threads and AI prompts were read in full. Five findings are fixed; the alias-progress request is declined with exact oracle evidence for both list buckets, context counts, alias and removed-selector configurations. The full status-registry source inventory is recorded in docs/ORACLE_REVIEW_ROUND12_FOLLOWUP_2026_11_13.md. Gates pass 442 library, 74 binary, 32 CLI dispatch, 12 admission, 7 identity and 163 differential tests (730 unique): claim/release 52, close 10, orientation 37, list 10, pagination 33, conformance 2, search/collections 17, output parity 2. Linux and Windows GNU cross-clippy, fmt and rustdoc pass. Instrumented library/binary tests pass; the new TOON reader measures 101/101 lines, 11/11 functions, 193/193 regions and 16/16 branch outcomes. This is scoped coverage; CI certifies the full aggregate and Windows execution. Thirteen distinct negative/restore scenarios, including copied passwords, default registry sources, numeric delimiter parsing, FIFO traversal/opening and table/session restoration, all fail with the relevant behavior removed and pass restored: 32 verified runs including final-reader repeats. Negatives fail assertions with exit 101; sources restore byte-identically. The linked PM six-test command passes without recording run artifacts. Every command remained below 1,200 seconds and used at most two jobs/test threads. No threshold, coverage scope or differential assertion was weakened. The oracle over-redacts quoted message decoration and rejects the delimiter example as an unknown-option path; both differences are pinned and documented. No finding is deferred and no review thread was replied to or resolved. The current npm latest is 2026.11.13; the accepted review oracle stays 2026.11.11."
  "2026-11-13T07:23:32.470Z",codex-agent,"Round 13: read the complete P1 thread and agent prompt. The renderer adds table controls only along object-only envelope paths and encodes arrays opaquely; item records and nested cell values never enter that traversal. Restore now follows the same structural boundary, pairs controls from array positions rather than suffix-scanning arbitrary fields, and never descends into expanded/restored rows. Envelope sibling control positions remain reserved as in the existing pre-encoded-table renderer contract; no escaping or wire-byte change is introduced. The new shared corpus covers all JSON kinds for labels_encoding, list_columns, null_columns, null_column_index and x_encoding, plus valid-looking instructions that must neither remove nor rewrite user data. Focused reader tests and the complete real-list oracle byte comparison pass. Literal prior-function revert proofs and the bounded TOON gates follow."
  "2026-11-13T08:09:28.935Z",codex-agent,"Round 13 complete: PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs62_AJu is fixed at the renderer boundary. Restore follows object-only envelope paths and never crosses an array edge into item data or decoded JSON cells; controls are paired from array positions rather than suffix-scanning user keys. Existing producer envelope control positions remain reserved, with no new escaping or output-byte change. All JSON kinds, including empty values, and valid-looking directives are preserved by the shared corpus. Full real-list stdout, stderr and status match the oracle, all decoded item values match JSON, and native checks still execute when the oracle is explicitly unavailable. Gates pass 18 selected TOON unit/session tests, 32 CLI dispatch, 12 admission, 7 identity and 164 differentials: claim/release 52, close 10, orientation 37, list 11, pagination 33, conformance 2, search/collections 17, output parity 2 (233 unique selected tests). Linux and Windows GNU cross-clippy and fmt pass. Scoped reader coverage is 99/99 lines, 12/12 functions, 190/190 regions and 18/18 branch outcomes. This is scoped evidence; CI certifies the aggregate and Windows runtime at unchanged thresholds. Three literal restore-function negative/restore pairs were replayed on final source: all negatives fail executed assertions with exit 101, all restorations pass, and copied sources restore byte-identically (six verified final runs). The linked PM selected tests pass without recording run artifacts. Every command stayed below 1,200 seconds with at most two jobs/test threads. Complete path audit and exact commands are in docs/ORACLE_REVIEW_ROUND13_2026_11_13.md. No differential assertion was weakened, no thread was replied to or resolved, and nothing is deferred."
  "2026-11-13T09:22:13.037Z",codex-agent,"Round 14: published 2026.11.11 accepts missing workflow sidecars for pause, start, atomic claim-start and close, both for an explicit missing mapping and an absent default. Four new differentials compare output and persisted item/history bytes; all pass. The ownership storage-fault contract now uses a directory at the mapped workflow path to retain a real I/O failure and its claim/journal guarantees. Reviewing repeated refusal formats, partial TOON column ordering and cross-target build-script discovery; the full Rust suite will run before push."
  "2026-11-13T09:27:51.286Z",codex-agent,"Focused review checks pass: the two repeated output-format orders match published refusal bytes; empty/partial TOON column-order hints preserve all delivered cells; host build-script discovery covers default and explicit-target layouts. Linux and Windows GNU all-target/all-feature clippy pass. The exact blank-evidence close command has byte-identical oracle/native recovery with no suggested retry; the policy and the existing unsupported update-evidence flags are recorded for follow-up at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/issues/167#issuecomment-6849115850. The full all-target Rust suite is running with a 45-minute cap."
  "2026-11-13T09:39:21.682Z",codex-agent,"Round 14 revert proof: isolated copies with literal starting-head json_requested, orientation_error_json, Workspace::deps, restore_row and own_build_scripts each fail the corresponding new executed regression, then pass after restoration. Reinstating the old ownership-contract expectation reproduces its assertion failure; the corrected storage-fault contract passes. A separate reject-missing-schema negative control fails all four lifecycle oracle tests and restoring fallback passes all four. The real explicit-target probe caught and corrected the first cache-marker guard; final host discovery passes the real target and synthetic layouts. All copied source/test bytes are restored. Linux and Windows GNU clippy, all-target check and fmt pass; the full final-source suite is running."
  "2026-11-13T09:58:39.425Z",codex-agent,"The native evidence-update gap is verified independently: published update with resolution, expected-result and actual-result exits 0; native rejects the dedicated resolution flag with exit 2. Searches found no existing issue-167 recovery item, so future compatibility work is tracked by open, unclaimed pm-rust-oracle-recovery-167 with the gh:unbraind/pm-rust#167 tag and linked evidence. The exact reported close command remains pinned to its published withdrawal policy."
  "2026-11-13T10:22:17.855Z",codex-agent,"Full all-target run reached its 2700-second cap in the search/collections target after 27 complete passing targets, including the corrected ownership contract; no test failed. The other lint, proof and linked-test processes are finished. Retrying both unfinished targets unfiltered, then repeating the full command without overlapping gates so the final report can distinguish a completed full pass from the bounded timeout."
  "2026-11-13T10:27:57.991Z",codex-agent,"Both unfinished targets pass unfiltered: search/collections 17 and strict JSON 3. All 29 targets have now completed successfully across bounded runs: 884 unique tests, 0 failures, 0 ignored, including all 170 differential tests and 12 admission contracts. This is complete target coverage, not a successful exit claim for the timed full command. The whole identical command is now retrying alone within the same 2700-second cap; the other test and lint processes are finished."
  "2026-11-13T11:02:27.458Z",codex-agent,"Final full-source retry passed: cargo test --locked -j2 --all-targets --all-features completed in 2057.2 seconds, below the 2700-second cap, with 884 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored across 29 test-bearing targets plus five zero-test examples. All 170 differentials, 12 admission contracts and 11 ownership contracts pass, including the original storage-fault failure. The prior full attempt timed out without an assertion failure; unchanged source passed this retry with the other gates finished. Eight isolated negative controls fail and pass after restoration; actual explicit-target build-script discovery passes. Linux and Windows GNU clippy, cargo check, fmt and the linked four workflow cases pass. Oracle accepts explicit/default missing workflows for all four mutations; real directory I/O faults and claim/journal guarantees remain tested. Three review findings are fixed; the reported blank-evidence retry retains oracle parity, with evidence and the separate native update-flag follow-up on issue 167 and pm-rust-oracle-recovery-167. Releasing this claim without closing either item; final changelog generation and checking follow."
  "2026-11-13T11:03:45.657Z",codex-agent,"Final delivery checks: the claim is released and this item remains in_progress; the recovery follow-up remains open and unclaimed. Changelog generation and changelog:check both pass after release. Recording this receipt, then regenerating/checking once more after this final tracker write. All 884 full-suite tests and 170 differentials pass; no assertion, coverage exclusion or threshold was weakened. Windows/macOS runtime and aggregate coverage remain for fresh CI. No review thread was replied to or resolved and no item was closed."
